Part 4 — Systemd Targets (Replaces Runlevels)

| Target            | Old Runlevel | Description                                 |
| ----------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| poweroff.target   | 0            | Halt the system                             |
| rescue.target     | 1            | Single-user, root shell, minimal services   |
| multi-user.target | 3            | Full multi-user, no GUI                     |
| graphical.target  | 5            | Full multi-user with GUI                    |
| emergency.target  | —            | Bare minimum: root shell, root fs read-only |
| reboot.target     | 6            | Reboot                                      |


4.1 — Check and Change the Default Target

# What target does the system boot into?
systemctl get-default

# List all active targets
systemctl list-units --type=target

# Set default to multi-user (no GUI)
sudo systemctl set-default multi-user.target

# Set it back to graphical
sudo systemctl set-default graphical.target

4.2 — Switch Targets Live (Without Reboot)

# Drop to multi-user (kills GUI session!)
sudo systemctl isolate multi-user.target

# Go back to graphical
sudo systemctl isolate graphical.target

# Enter rescue mode (needs root password)
sudo systemctl isolate rescue.target

# Enter emergency mode (root fs is read-only!)
sudo systemctl isolate emergency.target

